The First House is the branch of the [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oreskian]] government dedicated to information dissemination and monitoring. All [[Phenomena/Althane/Printing Press|printing presses]] and writing houses are registered with the First House, and the Oreskian post is inspected by members before it's allowed to be delivered. Ostensibly, the department works to keep state secrets from passing into the hands of their enemies.

Its officers wear deep blue, and among the highest of them is General [[People/Althane/Karkov|Yuri Karkov]]. He raised two wards, the orc [[People/Althane/Rampart|Rampart]] and the elven [[People/Althane/The Slipseer|Slipseer]], and kept them as lieutenants; both held ultra-violet clearance, and both are now dead. The House has named [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] the terrorists who killed its people at [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], broke its beacon and stole the [[Phenomena/Althane/The Gun|gun]] it had kept. Karkov called that gun the House's best chance at ridding the sphere of outward influence, and flyers of the Weft's faces went across Oresk to see them hunted down and hanged in the streets. Karkov was killed at [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], shot with the House's own gun, and the [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|Deep]] reached through a portal and took his body away before the Weft could claim it. The House raised [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]]'s war against it: he breaks into its offices and safe houses to steal medicine and to keep Sparrow refuges from being found.

Much of the House's work is done in research complexes buried under unmarked office buildings, several of them in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Kirov|Kirov]] and [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Sarengrad|Sarengrad]]. The largest of these, [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/RC3|RC3]], lies under an unmarked office building in Sarengrad. A visitor reaches one through a badge scanned by a guard, then a spirit print taken in a back room, then a second checkpoint equipped with the Liar's Downfall, a waterfall of real water enchanted to strip enchantment from anyone passing through it, and then an elevator down. The complex below is divided by clearance: a badge is cut for one tier, from red at the least through orange, yellow, green, blue and violet up to ultraviolet, which the heads of the House alone hold and which opens the whole facility. The House keeps its own repository of information on the people of Oresk, harder to reach than any complex.

Its city operations run from a building in the north of Sarengrad, near a well the [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Sparrows]] traced many fever cases to. The House does not want the [[Phenomena/Althane/Wasting Fever|wasting fever]] cured, and it has grown bolder against those who try. It has also been active around the corpse of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]], and had lately increased its work in the mountains near it, sending the Sparrows' own operative away without a word back.
